'''Lamasana''' ({{Langx|mxi|لَامَاسَانَا|Lamasána}}; {{Literal translation|sour apples}}'';'' {{Langx|kp|Itajaí}}) is an urban [[communes of Balisca|commune]] within the [[Camaca|Kamakã]] region of [[Bayara]]. It is the third most populous city in Bayara (after [[Macaio]] and ahead of [[Uxiu]]), and the [[List of Balisca cities by population|twenty-first most populous city]] in the [[Baliscan Confederation]], with a population of 584,363 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]]. 

Lamasana is located in the southern extremity of the [[Western Plains (Balisca)|Bayaran Plains]], in the foothills of the [[Matarrañya]].

